{"id":"384b518b-2f88-4c07-8f2d-82429bb44eae","object":"chat.completion","created":1793847827,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Apply the logger and stats consumer edits, then run the full test suite.\n\n```python\nr = replace_text_batch(\n    \"deepinfer/logger.py\",\n    [\n        {\n            \"old_text\": \"\"\"    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n\"\"\",\n            \"new_text\": \"\"\"    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n        *,\n        max_message_chars: int | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if (\n                isinstance(max_message_chars, bool)\n                or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int)\n                or max_message_chars < 32\n            ):\n                raise ValueError(\"max_message_chars must be an integer >= 32 or None\")\n        self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n\"\"\",\n        },\n        {\n            \"old_text\": \"\"\"    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        msg = super().format(record)\n        # 快速路径：单行日志（绝大多数情况）无需做对齐处理\n        if \"\\\\n\" in msg and record.message:\n            prefix = msg[: msg.find(record.message)]\n            msg = msg.replace(\"\\\\n\", \"\\\\n\" + prefix)\n        if self.use_color:\n            color = _LEVEL_COLORS.get(record.levelno)\n            if color:\n                msg = f\"{color}{msg}{_COLOR_RESET}\"\n        return msg\n\"\"\",\n            \"new_text\": \"\"\"    def _truncate_message(self, message: str) -> str:\n        if self.max_message_chars is None or len(message) <= self.max_message_chars:\n            return message\n        omitted = \"...<omitted>...\"\n        available = self.max_message_chars - len(omitted)\n        head = (available + 1) // 2\n        tail = available - head\n        return message[:head] + omitted + (message[-tail:] if tail else \"\")\n\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        message = record.getMessage()\n        if getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            message = self._truncate_message(message)\n        # 使用副本，避免当前 handler 的截断影响同一记录的其他 handler。\n        work_record = logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)\n        work_record.msg = message\n        work_record.args = ()\n        msg = super().format(work_record)\n        runtime_message = work_record.message\n        # 快速路径：单行日志（绝大多数情况）无需做对齐处理\n        if \"\\\\n\" in msg and runtime_message:\n            prefix = msg[: msg.find(runtime_message)]\n            msg = msg.replace(\"\\\\n\", \"\\\\n\" + prefix)\n        if self.use_color:\n            color = _LEVEL_COLORS.get(record.levelno)\n            if color:\n                msg = f\"{color}{msg}{_COLOR_RESET}\"\n        return msg\n\"\"\",\n        },\n        {\n            \"old_text\": \"\"\"    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n    )\n\"\"\",\n            \"new_text\": \"\"\"    from deepinfer import envs\n\n    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n        max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS,\n    )\n\"\"\",\n        },\n    ],\n    r_log[\"file_hash\"],\n)\nprint(\"logger edit:\", r)\n\nr2 = replace_text_batch(\n    \"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\",\n    [\n        {\n            \"old_text\": \"\"\"            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m)\n\"\"\",\n            \"new_text\": \"\"\"            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})\n\"\"\",\n        }\n    ],\n    r_st[\"file_hash\"],\n)\nprint(\"stats edit:\", r2)\n\ncheck = run_command([\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"])\nprint(\"pytest rc:\", check[\"rc\"])\nprint(check[\"stdout\"])\nprint(check[\"stderr\"])\nif check[\"rc\"] == 0:\n    final_answer(\"Implemented environment-controlled diagnostic log truncation while keeping stats logs complete; full pytest suite passes.\")\n```","reasoning_content":"We need continue. Last request number 19, max 20, only 1 left after response. Must be efficient: apply edits to logger.py and stats_logger.py, verify pytest, create patch.diff/run.log? Need final_answer. Environ already edited. Need inspect env change maybe fine. Need read logger relevant lines already exposed. Need apply edits with anchors known. We have logger content hash. Need perhaps read exact regions to craft precise replacements. We have full logger read earlier, but not content in current context except evidence chunks. Need exact formatter __init__ and format. We have them from evidence ev-307... lines 33-68 complete. Need after line 68? format body ends return msg then _root_logger. We can construct replacement of __init__, and format method. Must also add helper. Existing imports include logging. Need careful design.\n\nNewLineFormatter signature:\ndef __init__(self, fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False, *, max_message_chars: int | None = None) -> None:\n validate: if max_message_chars is not None: isinstance(bool) -> ValueError; not isinstance(int) or <32 -> ValueError. Message perhaps \"max_message_chars must be an integer >= 32 or None\". No env var needed here.\n set self.max_message_chars.\n\nNeed truncate after interpolation, without mutating record. logging.Formatter.format does interpolation and sets record.message, record.exc_text, etc. Problem: super().format(record) uses record.message and may mutate record.message? Let's recall logging.Formatter.format: record.message = record.getMessage(). Then s = self.formatMessage(record). Then exception appended to s. So truncating post super().format would truncate whole string including prefix and exception. Requirement budget only message body, not prefix/exc/stack_info. Better implement logic before super().format: derive rendered message without mutating record. `message = record.getMessage()` (doesn't mutate except record.message? LogRecord.getMessage: msg = str(self.msg); if self.args: msg = msg % self.args; return msg. Does not set record.message). Then if truncation and not keep_full: `message = self._truncate(message)`. Need make super().format use truncated message without mutating shared record's msg/args. Could temporarily set `record.message`? logging.Formatter.format sets `record.message = record.getMessage()` unconditionally, overwrites. Cannot feed message. Options:\n\n- Call super().format(record) after temporarily setting `record.msg = truncated` and args = ()? But mutating shared record prohibited, and could restore in finally, but handlers sequentially and need full for later handler. Temporarily mutating then restore might be considered \"不能改写共享原记录的 msg、args、exc_info、stack_info\". Better avoid.\n\n- Implement formatting manually copying logging.Formatter.format, using message. Or use a proxy record copy? Could create `logging.LogRecord` clone with same fields: `record_copy = logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)` or copy.copy(record), then set copy.msg=truncated, args=(). Then call super().format(copy). But record.exc_info and stack_info included; record_copy references same exception but format doesn't mutate original. However `super().format(copy)` sets copy.message, copy.exc_text. Original unaffected except? copy.copy shallow. This is good. But requirement \"沿用原有多行前缀、时间精度、颜色及异常处理\". Copy works.\n\nNeed also ensure record.message maybe already set from another handler? We should use record.getMessage() directly. To get correct formatting with format string, create copy.\n\nCould implement:\ndef format(self, record):\n    msg = self._format_with_message(record)\n...\ndef _format_with_message:\n   max_chars = self.max_message_chars\n   full = getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True\n   message = record.getMessage()\n   if max_chars is not None and not full:\n       message = self._truncate_message(message, max_chars)\n   if message == record.getMessage()? Always clone maybe only when truncate? If no truncation call super().format(record) preserves exact behavior. But if no truncation and record.message absent, super does same. For truncation path, clone and set msg. However if record.message set by prior handler? Super format ignores existing message? It resets. Good.\n   if truncated:\n      r = logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)\n      r.msg = message\n      r.args = ()\n      # perhaps r.message = message? super resets.\n      return super().format(r)\n   return super().format(record)\nBut this calls record.getMessage() twice? Fine. But note if args mapping etc. We rendered. `logging.makeLogRecord` copies dict, then call super().format(copy) sets copy.message truncated, but exc_info/ stack_info copied. Good. Exception text maybe record.exc_text cached in dict; copy owns string. Original not modified. For non-truncated, super may mutate original record.message and exc_text as usual. Requirement says cannot rewrite shared original record's msg,args,exc_info,stack_info - normal logging mutates message/exc_text but not prohibited fields. Fine.\n\nBut requirement \"先完成 %s 等参数替换，再计算消息长度\" yes.\n\nTruncate algorithm: marker = \"...<omitted>...\" length 15. budget >=32. remaining = budget - 15 (e.g. 17). start = ceil(remaining/2) = (remaining +1)//2 =9, end=remaining-start=8. return message[:start] + marker + (message[-end:] if end else \"\"). `len` Unicode code points. Good.\n\nMulti-line prefix logic uses record.message. In our format, after super, we currently check `if \"\\n\" in msg and record.message:`. But for truncation path, we formatted copy and original record.message may remain previous None or stale. Need align prefix from actual formatted message. Could use `message` variable. Need modify format to know rendered message. E.g.\ndef format(self, record):\n    rendered = self._message_for_record(record)\n    if rendered is not None: # truncated\n       working = logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)\n       working.msg = rendered\n       working.args = ()\n       msg = super().format(working)\n       message = working.message\n    else:\n       msg = super().format(record)\n       message = record.message\n    if \"\\n\" in msg and message: ...\nColor...\nBut simpler even non-budget always use copy and set msg=rendered,args=(). That guarantees no original mutation and uses message var. Is there any downside? Copy loses custom subclass methods? `logging.makeLogRecord` returns LogRecord, not subclass, but format only uses standard attrs. Some custom fields preserved. But tests may check original record fields unchanged. Good. However exception `exc_info` copied. The `format` implementation may call record.exc_text set on copy. Requirement preserve. But one concern: `logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)` invokes LogRecord constructor with keys as kwargs, which may include `message` causing? makeLogRecord:\nrv = LogRecord(None, None, \"\", 0, \"\", (), None, None)\nrv.__dict__.update(dict)\nreturn rv\nSo fine.\n\nBut using copy unconditionally may mean original record.message isn't set by formatter. Some existing behavior? Tests perhaps check NewLineFormatter outputs normal. Fine. But requirement \"保留原有...\" okay.\n\nHowever original `format` prefix calculation uses `record.message` which is exact final message after interpolation. With copy, `work.message` same. Good.\n\nWe need perhaps add import copy? Use logging.